	(text_box "BOOT OPTION PINS\n\nPins to watch for, that might affect boot options before fuse is blown:\nEIM_DA1 = BOOT_CFG1[1] (likely 0 from RTL chip) (BT_WAKE)\nEIM_DA6 = BOOT_CFG1[6] (1 = SD/eMMC, 0 = SerialROM) (BT_DIS: 10k pulled up) (prevents serialrom)\nEIM_WAIT = BOOT_CFG4[1] (ignore: i2c selector)\n\nSerial ROM:\nBOOT_CFG1[7] = 0\nBOOT_CFG1[6] = 0\nBOOT_CFG1[5] = 1\nBOOT_CFG1[4] = 1\n(SDR12)\nBOOT_CFG3[2] = 0 (792MHz ARM, 528MHz DDR)\nBOOT_CFG3[7-4] = 00 (MMU and cache disable, all good)\n\neMMC:\nBOOT_CFG1[7] = 0\nBOOT_CFG1[6] = 1\nBOOT_CFG1[5] = 1\nBOOT_CFG1[1] = 0    eMMC doesnt use reset pin\nBOOT_CFG2[1] = ?    eMMC boot ack enable\nBOOT_CFG2[4:3] = (10 for SDHC3) !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\nBOOT_CFG2[5-7] = 000 (1bit data is ok)\nBOOT_CFG3 same as above\n\nSD:\nBOOT_CFG1[7] = 0\nBOOT_CFG1[6] = 1\nBOOT_CFG1[5] = 0\n(SD speed normal SDR12)\nBOOT_CFG2 00s\n(SDHC1 + 1bit)\nBOOT_CFG3 same as above"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.12 50.8 0)
		(size 86.36 76.2)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
